  "latest_local_commit": "097b11d Record S4C-inspired validation control",
  "gpu_visibility_note": "Full-access session exposes /dev/nvidia0, /dev/nvidiactl, /dev/nvidia-uvm and nvidia-smi sees an NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell (driver 580.173.02); torch 2.13.0+cu130 reports cuda_available=true, device_count=1, compute capability 12.0. Earlier no-GPU reports were container passthrough failures, not physical GPU absence.",
  "scientific_status": "Synthetic P0 passes in two seeds. The official FlatLands split fails scene isolation. The non-official upstream-provenance split passes full integrity, a 512-scene bounded mask/query gate, direct-ZIP replay, and validation-only baselines. Three completion seeds, K=32/64/128 convergence, a PaSCo-inspired three-subnet same-contract control with K-sensitivity, a three-seed independent-decoder control, a three-seed deterministic posterior mean-map control, a three-seed S4C-inspired coordinate-query control, and four-method reliability/selective-risk curves are now complete on validation; the public site adds real-checkpoint qualitative and calibration diagnostics while test remains locked. The capacity-matched F=16 ConPath main model averages 0.09607 +/- 0.01222 exact Brier across three seeds, versus 0.11214 +/- 0.00306 for the independent decoder, 0.09204 +/- 0.00582 for the S4C-inspired coordinate control, and 0.07111 +/- 0.00377 for binary mean-map events; the mean-map hidden-cell Brier is 0.17842 +/- 0.00512, so all remain validation-only diagnostics, not final paper results. The official ORFD semantics audit is complete as a ground-vehicle second-domain candidate, but its image-plane labels do not yet support a same-contract metric-BEV event result. UnScenes3D is now the priority second-domain candidate: its one-scene raw pose smoke package is acquired, while labels/maps and the metric-BEV adapter remain pending.",
  "active_task": "Replace the desk-surface pilot with a ground-robot/floor visual, then finish the UnScenes3D label/local-map, coordinate, and sequence-held-out adapter checks before any test access or final site claim. Official FlatLands, SceneSense, and ORFD artifact/contract audits are recorded; FlatLands and SceneSense remain reference-only, ORFD has no local run, and UnScenes3D raw smoke is not a result.",
